{
  "dom_id": "step-q175955",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Expressed as an improper fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{2}{5}\\times 7=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe divide and multiply, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{2}{5}\\times 7 & = \\\\ (\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{2}{5})\\times 7 & = \\\\ (\\frac{3}{7}\\times \\frac{5}{2})\\times 7 & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 5}{7\\times 2}\\times 7 & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{14}\\times 7 & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{14}\\times \\frac{7}{1} & = \\\\ \\frac{15\\times 7}{14\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{105}{14} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
